# Termite anchor traffic (#587), after Roth 2005 section 4.4.1: each source sends
# one 64-byte packet every 0.5 s (1024 bit/s) to a partner fixed at the start,
# and the partner answers (the dissertation's per-packet acknowledgement, here a
# reply flow at the same rate). 10 pairs of the 100 nodes, drawn with
# random.Random(4).sample(range(100), 20); flows start at 60 s (the section's
# initial equilibrium pause) and run to the end.
# src dst start stop cbrBps
